 "notes": "Ledger grid is on the RIGHT page (p.127, header \"CHART THIRTEEN\"); printed explanatory sentences are on the LEFT page (p.126). Year printed above DATE = 1939; no year change mid-chart. Requested crop files (c-71-LT/LB/RT/RB) did not exist, so all crops were generated from c-71.png (3811x2783).\n\nColumn layout verified by detecting the 19 vertical grid lines (x \u2248 2019,2114,2209,2307,2401,2495,2593,2685,2787,2883,2982,3065,3173,3271,3369,3458,3554,3643,3741). US=cols1-6, BS=cols7-12, KP=cols13-18, each ordered SR,NR,UT,DT,NRC,SRC. DT columns have red left borders.\n\nEvery triple where US, BS and KP all appear satisfies KP = US + BS (all checksums pass), which anchored several fraction reads: BS Sept 2 is 70 3/8 (not 70 7/8) since 55 1/4+70 3/8=125 5/8; US Sept 2 is 55 1/4 (not 55 1/8); BS Sept 18 is 83 3/4 (not 83 1/4) since 70 1/2+83 3/4=154 1/4; BS Sept 14 is 91 3/4 since 76 3/8+91 3/4=168 1/8.\n\nColumn assignments match the printed annotations: Aug 29/Sept 1 = Natural Rally; Sept 2-12 = Upward Trend (peak pivots underlined red at BS 100 on Sept 11 and US 82 3/4 / KP 182 3/4 on Sept 12); Sept 14-18 = Natural Reaction (low pivots underlined red on Sept 18); Sept 19-20 = Natural Rally; Sept 28-Oct 4 = Secondary Reaction; Oct 6 = Secondary Rally. Sept 12 has no BS entry (KP 182 3/4 = US 82 3/4 + carried BS 100).\n\nDate labels: SAT-prefixed rows are Saturdays (confirmed: Sept 1 1939 = Friday, so Aug 26 = Saturday). Monday Sept 4 (Labor Day) is skipped, so SAT.2 is followed by row 5. No Sunday rows.\n\nHeader anomaly: the top DT carried-pivot triple 43 1/4 / 50 1/4 / 93 7/8 does NOT checksum (43 1/4+50 1/4 = 93 1/2 vs written 93 7/8) \u2014 expected for independent carried-forward pivots, transcribed as written. In the lower (1939-band) carried row, US 41 5/8 and KP 93 1/2 are red in the DOWNWARD TREND column, but the matching BS value 51 7/8 physically sits in the BS NATURAL REACTION column and is blue ink (though 41 5/8+51 7/8=93 1/2); flagged uncertain and transcribed by actual position/color.",
